BS_:

BU_: Vector__XXX

CM_ "Fiat Punto 188 (Mk2) 1.2 8V Fire - B-CAN 50 kbps, 11-bit IDs. Listen-only reverse engineering 2026-11-21/25 (ESP32-S3 + OBD-II K-Line ground truth). Transmitters not asserted (Vector__XXX throughout): sniffing cannot prove who sends what. 0x0C6/0x0C7 intentionally excluded - UDS-style visitors, suspected diagnostic-tool traffic, never native. ENGINE ON = RPM > 0 (0DD.b0/b1 == 0 is NOT a valid engine-on test: it also appears transiently at key-on). Confirmed here only; unverified hypotheses (odometer candidate in 743, warning lamps, 0DD.b4:b5 injection, 0E5.b3, 702.b1) live in docs/FINDINGS.md - do not treat as signals.";

BO_ 221 Punto_Engine: 7 Vector__XXX
 SG_ RPM : 48|8@1+ (32,0) [0|8160] "rpm" Vector__XXX
 SG_ Coolant : 16|8@1+ (1,-40) [-40|215] "degC" Vector__XXX
 SG_ LoadRaw : 32|8@1+ (1,0) [0|255] "" Vector__XXX
CM_ SG_ 221 RPM "0DD.b6 * 32. Equivalent to the 1.4 16V design (byte 6 = rpm, x32) and fits OBD 010C on par or better than a 16-bit b6:b5 read. Do NOT treat b5 as the RPM low byte - it is a separate byte (see FINDINGS injection hypothesis).";
CM_ SG_ 221 Coolant "0DD.b2 - 40, exact-law RMSE 0.2-0.5C over 37-87C.";
CM_ SG_ 221 LoadRaw "0DD.b4, raw high byte. 0-10 observed when read alone; correlates with OBD load (0104, r~0.84). Suspected high byte of a 16-bit injection/consumption field b4:b5 (unverified - see FINDINGS).";

BO_ 240 Punto_Body: 8 Vector__XXX
 SG_ Handbrake : 5|1@1+ (1,0) [0|1] "" Vector__XXX
 SG_ DoorDrv : 10|1@1+ (1,0) [0|1] "" Vector__XXX
 SG_ DoorPsg : 11|1@1+ (1,0) [0|1] "" Vector__XXX
 SG_ DoorRearLeft : 12|1@1+ (1,0) [0|1] "" Vector__XXX
 SG_ DoorRearRight : 13|1@1+ (1,0) [0|1] "" Vector__XXX
 SG_ BootOpen : 14|1@1+ (1,0) [0|1] "" Vector__XXX
 SG_ EngineStopped : 19|1@1+ (1,0) [0|1] "" Vector__XXX
 SG_ StandbyAsleep : 20|1@1+ (1,0) [0|1] "" Vector__XXX
 SG_ IgnitionOn : 22|1@1+ (1,0) [0|1] "" Vector__XXX
 SG_ Cranking : 23|1@1+ (1,0) [0|1] "" Vector__XXX
 SG_ FuelSender : 40|8@1+ (1,0) [0|100] "percent" Vector__XXX
CM_ SG_ 240 StandbyAsleep "0F0.b2 bit4. Whole byte is a clean state ladder: 0x10 asleep -> 0x48 key-on/engine-off -> 0xC8 cranking -> 0x40 running.";
CM_ SG_ 240 EngineStopped "0F0.b2 bit3 (0x08). Set at key-on while the engine is not turning.";
CM_ SG_ 240 IgnitionOn "0F0.b2 bit6 (0x40). Set at key-on (MAR) and stays set while running.";
CM_ SG_ 240 Cranking "0F0.b2 bit7 (0x80). Verified to the millisecond against first RPM>0 in the key-on captures.";
CM_ SG_ 240 FuelSender "Provisional scale ~percent: 24-27 quarter tank, 43-48 half tank, monotonic rise during fill, leads the damped cluster gauge. Brim-fill lock pending (expect ~95-100).";

BO_ 229 Punto_Speed: 4 Vector__XXX
 SG_ Speed : 7|16@0+ (0.1,0) [0|300] "kmh" Vector__XXX
 SG_ BusAwake : 22|1@1+ (1,0) [0|1] "" Vector__XXX
 SG_ UnknownB3 : 24|8@1+ (1,0) [0|255] "" Vector__XXX
CM_ SG_ 229 BusAwake "0E5.b2 bit6 (0x40): 0x00 while the network is asleep, 0x40 once awake.";
CM_ SG_ 229 UnknownB3 "Fast-moving, uncorrelated with RPM/throttle/load/MAP. Verified NOT a pure checksum of b0..b2 (non-deterministic from them alone while moving) yet constant 0x23 for 2000+ stationary frames. Unresolved - see FINDINGS.";

BO_ 207 Punto_Lights: 6 Vector__XXX
 SG_ FootBrake : 7|1@1+ (1,0) [0|1] "" Vector__XXX
 SG_ LightFog : 9|1@1+ (1,0) [0|1] "" Vector__XXX
 SG_ LightLow : 11|1@1+ (1,0) [0|1] "" Vector__XXX
 SG_ LightHigh : 12|1@1+ (1,0) [0|1] "" Vector__XXX
 SG_ LightPosA : 13|1@1+ (1,0) [0|1] "" Vector__XXX
 SG_ LightPosB : 14|1@1+ (1,0) [0|1] "" Vector__XXX
 SG_ Defog : 20|1@1+ (1,0) [0|1] "" Vector__XXX
 SG_ BlinkRight : 21|1@1+ (1,0) [0|1] "" Vector__XXX
 SG_ BlinkLeft : 22|1@1+ (1,0) [0|1] "" Vector__XXX
CM_ SG_ 207 LightPosA "Sidelights use bits 5+6 together (b1=0x60); why two bits is unknown but they always move together.";
CM_ SG_ 207 BlinkRight "File-confirmed 2026-11-22 (0x00<->0x20 at blink rate). Hazard = 0x60.";

BO_ 243 Punto_HandbrakeEcho: 3 Vector__XXX
 SG_ Handbrake : 5|1@1+ (1,0) [0|1] "" Vector__XXX

BO_ 242 Punto_Buttons: 1 Vector__XXX
 SG_ City : 5|1@1+ (1,0) [0|1] "" Vector__XXX

BO_ 1792 Punto_Nm0: 4 Vector__XXX
CM_ BO_ 1792 "B-CAN network management heartbeat. b1: 0x1A sleep, 0x5A/0x9A wake bursts, 0x1E awake (bit 0x04 = awake); bit 0x10 mirrors stalk lights (0x1E off / 0x0E on). b3 ladder 0x01 -> 0x09 -> 0x0F (0x0F = configured/awake).";

BO_ 1793 Punto_Nm1: 2 Vector__XXX
CM_ BO_ 1793 "B-CAN NM heartbeat, only present while awake. b1 0x04 (asleep) -> 0x06 (awake). Static 00 06 otherwise.";

BO_ 1794 Punto_Nm2: 2 Vector__XXX
CM_ BO_ 1794 "B-CAN NM heartbeat. b1 was 0x06 on 2026-11-22 and 0x16 on 2026-11-24 - a single bit-4 flip. Suspected NM status bit or a slow counter (unverified - see FINDINGS watchlist).";

BO_ 1795 Punto_Nm3: 2 Vector__XXX
CM_ BO_ 1795 "B-CAN NM heartbeat, also broadcast while asleep. b1 0x1A (asleep) -> 0x1E (awake).";

BO_ 1856 Punto_KeyOnPing: 0 Vector__XXX
CM_ BO_ 1856 "One-shot zero-length frame at key-on, ~1 s after MAR, immediately preceding 0x743. Payload/meaning unverified.";

BO_ 1859 Punto_KeyOnHandshake: 6 Vector__XXX
CM_ BO_ 1859 "One-shot key-on handshake, fires ~1 s after MAR (1 ms after 0x740). Observed payload 46 76 89 95 AA A0 once per key cycle. Content NOT decoded - suspected central immobilizer/PROXI and/or odometer sync. Odometer candidate is a HYPOTHESIS only: see docs/FINDINGS.md watchlist.";
